  "title": "Bulls Land 2-Time All-Star Vucevic &amp; Aminu In Exchange For Cater Jr, Porter Jr, &amp; Two-First Round Picks",
  "htmlContent": "<!<span style=\"font-size:0px; color:#ff0000;\">﻿\n</span>-- wp:image {\"id\":510839,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"http://landonbuford.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/GettyImages-1299368190-683x1024.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-510839\"/><figcaption>ORLANDO, FLORIDA - JANUARY 29: Nikola Vucevic #9 of the Orlando Magic shoots a three pointer during the second quarter against the LA Clippers at Amway Center on January 29, 2021 in Orlando, Florida. NOTE TO USER: User expressly acknowledges and agrees that, by downloading and or using this photograph, User is consenting to the terms and conditions of the Getty Images License Agreement. (Photo by Douglas P. DeFelice/Getty Images)</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Orlando Magic trade all-star center Nikola Vucevic and Al-Farouq Aminu to the Chicago Bulls, sources t<a href=\"https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/31133908/orlando-magic-trade-nikola-vucevic-chicago-bulls-sources-say\">old ESPN's Adrian Wojnarowski on Thursday</a>.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The Bulls send Wendell Carter Jr., Otto Porter Jr., and two first-round picks in 2021 and 2023 to Magic, sources told ESPN.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Vucevic, averaging a career-high 24.5 points and 11.8 rebounds this season while shooting 40.6% from 3 points, is a considerable addition to the Bulls. The move also shows first-time All-Star Zach LaVine, that the Bulls want to improve their team to make it better.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The B<span style=\"font-size:0px; color:#ff0000;\">﻿\n</span>ulls are currently 19-24 and in tenth place in the Eastern Conference.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
  "excerpt": "-- wp:image {\"id\":510839,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --> ORLANDO, FLORIDA - JANUARY 29: Nikola Vucevic #9 of the Orlando Magic shoots a three pointer during the second quarter…",
